, containing high fat, protein, and iron. Duck has been hunted in the wild for thousands of years, and has been domesticated and bred for more than two thousand years, resulting in several breeds with varying characteristics."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-duck-as-food"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duck_as_food"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Beijing cuisine","cuisine/beijing-cuisine",[["Peking duck","dish/peking-duck"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Allium fistulosum","ingredient/allium-fistulosum"],["Spring pancake","ingredient/spring-pancake"],["Tianmianjiang","ingredient/tianmianjiang"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/29/And_%2824559569447%29.jpg/500px-And_%2824559569447%29.jpg","w":500,"h":332,"by":"cyclonebill from Copenhagen, Denmark","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:And_(24559569447).jpg"}},"dish/pepernoot":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pepernoot","n":"Pepernoot","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Dutch cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["A pepernoot is a Dutch cookie-like confectionery, traditionally associated with the early December Sinterklaas holiday in the Netherlands and Belgium. The ingredients have some similarities with German Pfeffernüsse."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pepernoot"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepernoot"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":10,"links":[["Anise","ingredient/anise"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Cloves","ingredient/cloves"],["Honey","ingredient/honey"],["Nutmeg","ingredient/nutmeg"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Rye flour","ingredient/rye-flour"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"